0	section	Setting out
0	section	Talking to Pirate Pete
1	line	Player	Hello there!
1	line	Pirate Pete	Mornin'.
1	line	Pirate Pete	Hey...you're an adventurer, right?
1	line	Player	Yes I am!
1	line	Player	Got any quests for me?
1	line	Pirate Pete	Yeah, I do, as a matter of fact!
1	line	Pirate Pete	(Ahem.)
1	line	Pirate Pete	I am a poor, dispossessed nobleman, forced by circumstance to lurk in the middle of nowhere, soliciting help from passers-by.
1	line	Pirate Pete	You see, my fiendish half-brother has seized my estates and forced me into exile.
1	line	Pirate Pete	The simple lemon farmers suffer under his tyrannous yoke, and only a brave adventurer can lift his iron boot from the neck of the poor.
1	line	Pirate Pete	To reclaim my lands I will need to have my family sword returned to me so that I may present it as proof of my rulership.
1	line	Pirate Pete	Will you help me find my family sword?
1	cond	If the player has one or more levels less than the requirement:
2	box	Before starting this quest, be aware that one or more of your skill levels are lower than what is required to fully complete it.
2	action	continues
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Yes!
2	line	Player	Yes! Your uncorroborated sob story has touched my heart. When do we set off?
2	line	Pirate Pete	You'll help! Wonderful!
2	line	Pirate Pete	But, alas, my half brother has a powerful ally, the mighty demon...
2	line	Pirate Pete	Err...
2	line	Pirate Pete	Err...Barrelor!
2	line	Player	Barrelor?
2	line	Pirate Pete	That's what I said!
2	line	Pirate Pete	Barrelor is an awesome opponent, and to reclaim my family sword you will need to defeat him, for he guards it within the deadly Trapped Pit of Barrelor.
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	Of course, I fear no demon!
3	line	Player	Of course, I fear no demon!
3	line	Pirate Pete	That's the spirit!
3	line	Pirate Pete	When I am reinstated in my rightful place, I will not be a very wealthy man, as my half-brother has squandered my family fortune.
3	line	Pirate Pete	However, I will gladly give you every bent penny of what is left, and starve in the gutter with my many, many adorable children, if you say you will help me.
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	Nonsense! Keep the money!
4	line	Player	Nonsense! Keep the money! I will dispose of this evil half-brother of yours and leave you what little money is left to feed your family.
4	line	Pirate Pete	Wonderful! Just pick up your diversion and we'll leave!
4	line	Player	What diversion?
4	line	Player	Ow!
4	action	(Cutscene 1 begins.)
3	option	Great, I'll take the cash in used coins please.
4	line	Player	Great, I'll take the cash in used coins please.
4	line	Pirate Pete	Er...
4	line	Pirate Pete	Look, I think I'll wait here for someone a little more... you know...
4	line	Pirate Pete	...heroic.
4	action	end
2	option	Not a chance, this sounds too dangerous.
3	line	Player	Not a chance, this sounds too dangerous.
3	line	Pirate Pete	Look, I think I'll wait here for someone a little more... you know...
3	line	Pirate Pete	...heroic.
3	action	end
1	option	No.
2	line	Player	No, I don't think I'll help you out this time.
2	line	Pirate Pete	Look, I think I'll wait here for someone a little more... you know...
2	line	Pirate Pete	...heroic.
2	action	end
