0	section	Cutscene 1
1	line	Captain Braindeath	Arrr... 'Tis lookin' bleak...
1	line	Pirate Pete	Cap'n!
1	line	Pirate Pete	Good news Cap'n!
1	line	Pirate Pete	I found us a hero down by the docks!
1	line	Captain Braindeath	Be they heroic, brave and true?
1	line	Pirate Pete	Aye! They also be gullible, tied up and unconscious!
1	line	Pirate Pete	They were willing to help out some random stranger with a good enough sob story, so I smacked them with a bottle and rowed them over.
1	line	Captain Braindeath	Brilliant! The island's location will remain a secret!
1	line	Captain Braindeath	Bring 'em here and wake 'em up.
1	line	Captain Braindeath	We may make it through this yet...
1	action	(Cutscene ends and dialogue continues below.)
0	section	Meeting Captain Braindeath
1	line	Captain Braindeath	Are ye alright, [lad/lass]?
1	line	Player	Ohhhh... My head...
1	line	Player	It feels like someone has smacked me one with a bottle...
1	line	Captain Braindeath	Arr... Those devils gave ye a nasty knock when ye came to aid us.
1	line	Captain Braindeath	But now yer here we'll run those evil brain-eatin' dogs off the island fer good!
1	line	Player	What? What is going on here?
1	line	Player	I can't seem to remember anything beyond chatting to a man at the docks.
1	line	Captain Braindeath	Arr. Well, [lad/lass], that would be Pete, one of my men.
1	line	Captain Braindeath	He's been out lookin' fer heroes like yerself to aid us in our peril.
1	line	Player	Okay... I'll buy that. It sounds like something I would do.
1	line	Player	So where am I, and what is going on?
1	line	Captain Braindeath	Yer on Braindeath Island!
1	line	Captain Braindeath	Where it lies is a secret, because ye are standin' in the brewery of Cap'n Braindeath, purveyor of the most vitriolic alcoholic beverages in the world!
1	line	Player	Wow!
1	line	Captain Braindeath	I am the notorious alchemist Cap'n Braindeath, and this whole operation be my idea!
1	line	Captain Braindeath	With my crew of sturdy, upright pirate brewers, we sail the seven seas, distributing cheap 'alcohol' to all and sundry.
1	line	Player	Oooh!
1	line	Captain Braindeath	These be dark times, though, [lad/lass]. See, a week ago we awoke to find ourselves beseiged.
1	line	Captain Braindeath	The lads and I have held them off so far, but 'tis only a matter of time before they sweep through the buildin' and put us all to the sword.
1	line	Player	Who?
1	line	Captain Braindeath	Them!
1	box	The captian points out of the window....
1	line	Player	Are they...
1	line	Player	...protesting?
1	line	Captain Braindeath	Arr, [lad/lass]! That they are!
1	line	Captain Braindeath	Day and night they seek to break our will with their chantin', and their singin' and their passive resistance!
1	line	Player	So, what do you want me to do?
1	line	Captain Braindeath	Well, me and the lads got our heads together and decided that if we can get their Cap'n drunk enough, perhaps they'll stop protestin'.
1	line	Captain Braindeath	If that happens, we'll slip out the back and set up shop somewhere else.
1	line	Player	Well, how can I help?
1	line	Captain Braindeath	Well, first of all, we need someone to go out the front and grow us some Blindweed.
1	line	Captain Braindeath	'Tis one of the ingredients of our 'rum'.
1	line	Captain Braindeath	The only problem is that those rottin' fiends have torn up and destroyed all but one of the Blindweed Patches.
1	line	Captain Braindeath	Here, [lad/lass]. I'll give ye the seed you'll need fer growin' the herb. Help yerself to the gardenin' equipment in the basement.
1	line	Captain Braindeath	I'll warn ye again that those devils are sat right on top of the patch.
1	line	Captain Braindeath	Try hecklin' 'em from a distance. Those Swabs may talk a good fight, but if ye can put a scare in 'em they'll keep out of yer way!
1	action	end
0	section	Getting your 'beer-ings'
0	section	Talking to Captain Braindeath again
1	line	Player	So...
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	What exactly do you want me to do?
2	line	Player	What exactly do you want me to do?
2	line	Captain Braindeath	Arr, well I want ye to get outside and grow some Blindweed.
2	line	Captain Braindeath	Best be careful, [lad/lass], fer them pirates will skin ye alive if they catch ye.
2	cond	If the player has lost the Blindweed seed:
3	line	Player	And what happens if I lose the seed?
3	line	Captain Braindeath	Then I'll have ye flogged, hung, slapped with a haddock and sent back out there to fight the zombie hordes with little more than harsh language!
3	cond	If the player has no inventory space:
4	line	Captain Braindeath	Come back and see me when ye ain't loaded down with stuff, and I'll give ye another.
4	action	end
3	cond	If the player has inventory space:
4	line	Captain Braindeath	Arr... Here, [lad/lass]. Just take this and get goin'!
4	action	(The player is handed another seed.)
3	action	end
1	option	Why do you talk like a pirate?
2	line	Player	Why do you talk like a pirate? Didn't you tell me you were an alchemist?
2	line	Captain Braindeath	Arr, [lad/lass], 'tis true.
2	line	Captain Braindeath	However, 'tis also true that I stumbled across the basic recipe fer my most potent of brews in a terrible alchemical accident.
2	line	Captain Braindeath	See, 'twas a dark and stormy night, and the wind was howlin' around the trees as I worked late into the night.
2	line	Captain Braindeath	Steppin' too close to a candle with my flask in my hand, I was suddenly swept up in a terrible, yet potently alcoholic, explosion.
2	line	Player	And?
2	line	Captain Braindeath	Well' [lad/lass], it seems the fumes from that first batch of me 'rum' did strange things to me brain.
2	line	Captain Braindeath	I don't remember the exact words the healers used, but apparently the stuff burned out the tiny, specialised part of me brain that tells me not to talk like a pirate.
2	line	Player	That... that... that sounds utterly impossible!
2	line	Captain Braindeath	Arr! That be what I told them!
2	action	end
1	option	So what do you make here anyway?
2	line	Player	So what do you make here anyway?
2	line	Captain Braindeath	'Rum', [lad/lass]!
2	line	Captain Braindeath	The finest, most potent, most flammable and most debilitatin' 'rum' in the whole of Gielinor!
2	line	Player	Rum, eh?
2	line	Captain Braindeath	No, [lad/lass], 'rum'!
2	line	Player	What's the difference?
2	line	Captain Braindeath	Well, see, it's like this.
2	line	Captain Braindeath	If we called the stuff we make 'rum' without makin' the little quote gestures every time, then the Cookin' Guild has promised to do entertaininly painful things to us with whisks.
2	line	Captain Braindeath	See, technically -
2	line	Captain Braindeath	And by that I mean technically according to the Disposal of Hazardous Waste Act and the Health and Safety Laws -
2	line	Captain Braindeath	technically, what we're brewin' here is Artificially Produced Hyper Condensed Sweetened 'Rum' Flavour Distillate.
2	line	Player	Riiiiiiiight...
2	line	Captain Braindeath	So ye see, [lad/lass], we just call it 'rum' because the real name be a bit of a mouthful.
2	line	Captain Braindeath	Want a drop?
2	line	Player	No thanks... I think I'll skip it for now.
2	action	end
